(property "Description" "Concrete BOM candidate: Delta BFB0305HA-C two-wire centrifugal blower. Factory red wire positive, black wire negative; no invented connector numbering. Mechanical integration and qualification remain open. | module | Maker PDF rev00 specifies5.0V nominal,4.5-5.5V operating,0.13A average nominal/0.20A maximum average,0.65W nominal/1.00W maximum; these are not startup peak ratings. The drawing label artwork also shows0.24A, so the design budget reserves0.25A continuous until the actual label/current is checked.; Use existing AO3400A low-side switch: this exact suffix has two wires and no tach output. Red=LAB5, black=switched return. Keep flyback SS14 and fit10uF plus100nF directly across the blower leads.; Provisional startup budget is0.50A, a project qualification limit rather than a manufacturer guarantee. Delta explicitly requires peak-current measurement with an oscilloscope. Capture starting/stalled/auto-restart current and LAB5 droop at both5V rail limits.; Manufacturer body envelope is30.0+/-0.5 by30.0+/-0.5 by10.0+/-0.5mm; mounting hole spacing24.0+/-0.3mm, two holesdiameter2.4+/-0.3mm; lead length145+/-10mm. Allocate at least32x32x12mm for the body as a design fit gate, plus intake/outlet duct clearance and lead strain relief.; Maker free-air airflow1.45CFM nominal/min1.17CFM and zero-flow pressure0.285inH2O nominal/min0.182inH2O are curve endpoints, not simultaneous installed performance. Qualify the separate display duct, inlet pressure drop<=5Pa, closed-cover thermal limits and RF noise. Operating range-10 to70C.; LAB5 aggregate, including concurrency with RTL-B, remains unqualified. If measured steady demand exceeds2.5A, follow STACK load-shedding/D36V50F5 plusfuse review before commissioning." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
